The server leaves a player's ammo to the player's client, which counts it as it fires
and says so in its snapshots; the reference has no client, so its server counts it, as
the client's TSprite.Fire does.

--- a/shared/mechanics/Sprites.pas
+++ b/shared/mechanics/Sprites.pas
@@ -4279,7 +4279,8 @@
   end;

   // Shouldn't we dec on server too?
-  {$IFNDEF SERVER}
+  // the reference: counted as a player's client counts it (tests/opensoldat)
+  {$IF TRUE}
   if Weapon.AmmoCount > 0 then
     Dec(Weapon.AmmoCount);
   {$ENDIF}
